WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.425
When the issuer is AD CS, the
infrastructure rules are strict.

2
00:00:04.425 --> 00:00:08.928
It needs an enterprise CA, and
the NDES and connector server must

3
00:00:08.928 --> 00:00:13.600
sit in the same forest, apart from
the CA and the domain controllers.

4
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:18.490
Here's the subtle one: the SCEP template
lets the request supply the subject,

5
00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:21.250
the very setting Module 1 calls dangerous.

6
00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:25.401
It's safe only while enrollment is
limited to the NDES service account,

7
00:00:25.401 --> 00:00:27.762
so audit that permission like any other,

8
00:00:27.762 --> 00:00:31.412
and keep the connector server in
the CA's administrative tier.

9
00:00:31.412 --> 00:00:35.225
NDES can't be clustered, so
run several identical servers,

10
00:00:35.225 --> 00:00:39.200
and watch its own certificates,
a frequent cause of outages.

11
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.712
Keep the connector current.

12
00:00:40.712 --> 00:00:43.916
As for which profile
fits which use, Wi-Fi,

13
00:00:43.916 --> 00:00:49.130
VPN and sign-in certificates use
SCEP, and the slide maps the rest.
